**Supported File Types:**
| Extension | Framework | Max Size |
|-----------|-----------|----------|
| .pkl, .joblib, .pickle | scikit-learn | 100 MB |
| .h5, .keras | TensorFlow/Keras | 500 MB |
| .pt, .pth | PyTorch | 500 MB |
| .onnx | ONNX Runtime | 500 MB |

**Response (201 Created):**
```json
{
  "id": "uuid-model-123",
  "project_id": "uuid-456",
  "name": "loan_model_v3",
  "description": "Logistic regression with feature engineering",
  "file_path": "/uploads/models/loan_model_v3.pkl",
  "file_size": 15728640,
  "model_type": "sklearn",
  "framework": "scikit-learn",
  "framework_version": "1.3.0",
  "model_class": "LogisticRegression",
  "features_count": 25,
  "created_at": "2026-02-05T15:30:00Z",
  "status": "ready"
}
```

**Frontend Implementation:**
```javascript
const uploadModel = async (projectId, modelFile, metadata) => {
  const formData = new FormData();
  formData.append('project_id', projectId);
  formData.append('name', metadata.name);
  formData.append('description', metadata.description);
  formData.append('file', modelFile);
  formData.append('model_type', metadata.modelType);
  formData.append('framework_version', metadata.frameworkVersion);

  const response = await fetch('/api/v1/models/upload', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${accessToken}`,
      // DON'T set Content-Type - browser sets it with boundary
    },
    body: formData,
    // Track upload progress
    onUploadProgress: (progressEvent) => {
      const percentCompleted = Math.round(
        (progressEvent.loaded * 100) / progressEvent.total
      );
      updateProgress(percentCompleted);
    }
  });

  return await response.json();
};
```

**Validation Rules:**
- File must be one of supported extensions
- File size must not exceed max limit
- Model must be loadable (backend validates)
- Name must be unique within project

**Error Codes:**
- 400: Invalid file format or validation error
- 413: File too large
- 415: Unsupported media type
- 422: Model file corrupted or unloadable

