## 📦 Supported Model Formats

### Model Loading Capabilities

| Framework | Extensions | Status | Notes |
|-----------|------------|--------|-------|
| **scikit-learn** | `.pkl`, `.joblib`, `.pickle` | ✅ Fully Supported | Most common format |
| **TensorFlow/Keras** | `.h5`, `.keras`, SavedModel dirs | ✅ Fully Supported | Requires TensorFlow installed |
| **PyTorch** | `.pt`, `.pth` | ✅ Fully Supported | Must be full model, not state_dict |
| **ONNX** | `.onnx` | ✅ Fully Supported | Cross-framework format |

### Model Type Detection

Backend automatically detects:
- Model framework
- Model class (e.g., LogisticRegression, RandomForest)
- Number of features expected
- Input/output shapes
- Framework version

**Frontend Responsibility:**
- Validate file extension before upload
- Show appropriate upload UI based on framework
- Display detected metadata after upload

### ⚠️ Known Limitations

| Limitation | Impact | Workaround |
|------------|--------|------------|
| PyTorch state_dict not supported | Upload fails | Save full model with `torch.save(model, path)` |
| Custom classes need definition | Loading fails | Include custom class in upload or use ONNX |
| TensorFlow < 2.0 deprecated | May fail | Upgrade to TensorFlow 2.x |
| Models > 500 MB | Upload times out | Compress or use ONNX format |

