## ⚠️ Error Handling

### HTTP Status Codes

| Code | Meaning | Frontend Action |
|------|---------|-----------------|
| 200 | OK | Display response data |
| 201 | Created | Show success message, redirect |
| 202 | Accepted | Start polling for completion |
| 400 | Bad Request | Show validation errors to user |
| 401 | Unauthorized | Redirect to login, refresh token |
| 403 | Forbidden | Show "Access Denied" message |
| 404 | Not Found | Show "Resource not found" |
| 409 | Conflict | Show conflict message (e.g., "Name already exists") |
| 413 | Payload Too Large | Show "File too large" error |
| 415 | Unsupported Media Type | Show "Invalid file type" error |
| 422 | Unprocessable Entity | Show detailed validation errors |
| 429 | Too Many Requests | Show "Rate limit exceeded", retry with backoff |
| 500 | Internal Server Error | Show generic error, contact support |
| 503 | Service Unavailable | Show "Service temporarily unavailable", retry |

### Error Response Format

```json
{
  "detail": "Validation error",
  "errors": [
    {
      "field": "password",
      "message": "Password must be at least 8 characters",
      "type": "value_error"
    },
    {
      "field": "email",
      "message": "Invalid email format",
      "type": "value_error"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Frontend Error Handling Example

```javascript
const handleAPIError = (error) => {
  if (error.response) {
    // Server responded with error status
    const { status, data } = error.response;

    switch (status) {
      case 400:
        // Validation errors
        if (data.errors) {
          data.errors.forEach(err => {
            showFieldError(err.field, err.message);
          });
        } else {
          showToast(data.detail, 'error');
        }
        break;

      case 401:
        // Unauthorized - try refresh token
        if (refreshToken) {
          await refreshAccessToken();
          // Retry original request
        } else {
          // No refresh token, redirect to login
          navigate('/login');
        }
        break;

      case 403:
        showToast('Access denied', 'error');
        break;

      case 404:
        showToast('Resource not found', 'error');
        break;

      case 409:
        showToast(data.detail, 'warning');
        break;

      case 413:
        showToast('File too large. Maximum size is 100 MB', 'error');
        break;

      case 422:
        showToast(data.detail, 'error');
        break;

      case 429:
        showToast('Too many requests. Please try again later', 'warning');
        // Implement exponential backoff
        break;

      case 500:
      case 503:
        showToast(
          'Service temporarily unavailable. Please try again',
          'error'
        );
        break;

      default:
        showToast('An unexpected error occurred', 'error');
    }
  } else if (error.request) {
    // Request made but no response
    showToast('Network error. Please check your connection', 'error');
  } else {
    // Something else happened
    showToast(error.message, 'error');
  }
};
```

